## 2. The suppliers I'd use for a genuinely custom room

For the first ten OddHobb Tiny Worlds, I would avoid custom injection moulding altogether.

| Part of the room              | Supplier approach                    | Why                                       |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |
| Walls, floors, windows        | Ponoko or another laser-cutting shop | Flat CAD-cut components, no mould costs   |
| Furniture and tiny objects    | JLC3DP                               | Custom resin miniatures from your meshes  |
| Wallpaper, books, photographs | Short-run digital printer            | Nearly unlimited personalisation          |
| Lighting                      | Standard low-voltage modules         | Avoid custom electronics initially        |
| Booklet and packaging         | Short-run printer + kitting partner  | Exact instructions and one gift-ready box |

Ponoko has no minimum order quantity or setup fee for standard laser-cutting designs and advertises prototype jobs from $50, but exact room-panel pricing requires uploading your CAD.&#x20;

